# THREE STATIONS, EACH SAYING WHERE THE PERSON IS TWICE — plan 26 `B3`.
#
# `feet` reads the WALKER. `plan` writes the picture and then reads the marker back
# OUT of it. The two lines are the same fact from opposite ends, and `run.sh`
# compares them — which is the only way to see that the plan draws the author the
# tick moved rather than a pose of its own.
#
# ⚠ THE STATIONS MUST DIFFER, and the probe checks that they do: a walker that never
# moved would let a marker hard-wired to the origin pass every row.

at 0 0 0
verb raise
feet
plan s1

# …and now the tick moves the person, which is the half a teleport cannot test.
keys 1
step 40
keys 0
feet
plan s2

# A yaw as well, so the facing has somewhere to point.
at 6 -3 90
feet
plan s3
